# ShapesOS — Docker build context (Phase 6). Keeps host state out of the
# image: `COPY . .` in the builder must never pick up a host node_modules
# (wrong-platform native binaries over the image's own `npm ci`), a local
# .env (secrets baked into a layer), or runtime data.

# dependencies + build output (the image installs and builds its own)
node_modules
**/node_modules
.next
out
build
*.tsbuildinfo

# secrets
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
*.pem
*.key
*.crt
*.p12
*.pfx

# runtime state (named volumes in docker-compose.yml)
.data
.run-artifacts
data
.pgdata
db-backups

# tests, tooling, VCS
.git
.github
.claude
coverage
test-results
playwright-report
scripts/e2e/report
scripts/e2e/.auth.json
scripts/e2e/.e2e-ids.json
screenshots
*.log
logs

# infra-as-code (render.yaml, the AWS CDK app): never part of an app image
infra
